<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Dexia CEO sees higher profit.</title>
<headline>Belgian Dexia CEO sees higher profit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Communal de Belgique (CCB), the Belgian arm of Belgian-French alliance Dexia, said on Monday that 1996 results were &quot;very favourable.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;CCB 1996 earnings will show a significant increase,&quot; chief executive officer Francois Narmon told a news conference.  </p>
<p>Narmon declined to comment on remarks by Pierre Richard, head of Dexia's French arm CLF, that he expected combined 1997 profits in excess of three billion French francs.</p>
<p>Final results for CCB are due on April 2.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
